    <!-- How to back up -->
    <string name="guide_title">How to back up your data</string>
    <string name="guide_intro">Your data lives only on this phone. A backup is a complete, encrypted copy you can use to restore everything if the phone is lost, broken, replaced or reset.</string>
    <string name="guide_1">Open Settings (the gear at the top right) → Security &amp; privacy → Back up to an encrypted file.</string>
    <string name="guide_2">Choose a strong backup password and write it down somewhere safe, away from your phone. It can\'t be recovered if forgotten.</string>
    <string name="guide_3">Choose where to save the file. Best is somewhere off this phone, such as Google Drive or a computer, so the backup survives if the phone is lost.</string>
    <string name="guide_4">Back up regularly. Each backup is a complete copy, so keep the newest one. The app reminds you when your last backup is getting old.</string>
    <string name="guide_5">To restore, on this phone or a new one: install the app, open Settings → Security &amp; privacy → Restore from a backup, pick the file and enter the password.</string>
    <string name="guide_tip">Backups are encrypted with AES-256. Without the password the file can\'t be opened by anyone, including the makers of the app.</string>

